   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe first file is the package entry point for exllamav3. It sets environment defaults before importing torch (disabling the ROCm profiler registration thread by default), raises a clear error if PyTorch isn't installed, and configures the CUDA caching allocator to use expandable segments (skipping Windows, ROCm, and user-configured setups). It also points Triton at the AMD backend on ROCm builds, then re-exports the library's main public API\u2014Config, Model, Tokenizer, Cache classes, Generator/Job types, and sampler utilities\u2014so users can import them directly from `exllamav3`."
  },
